.TH FALLOCATE 2 "2026-09-06" "EpinAnonymOS" "System Calls"
.SH NAME
fallocate \- Linux syscall 285, as implemented by the EpinAnonymOS kernel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B syscall(285, ...)
.br
kernel handler: \fBlinux_sys_fallocate\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
fallocate(fd, mode, offset, len). Weston's wl_shm allocator (toytoolkit /
os_create_anonymous_file) does memfd_create → F_SEAL_SHRINK → posix_fallocate,
which issues fallocate(fd, 0, 0, size). Without this the clients can't size
their shared buffers ("creating a buffer file … failed: Function not
implemented") and nothing draws. For our memfd-backed buffers, "allocate
space up to offset+len" is exactly ftruncate-grow (which allocates the
physical pages). Hole-punch / other FALLOC_FL_* modes are accepted as no-ops.
.SH IMPLEMENTATION
Dispatched from \fIsrc/kernel/d/core/kernel_main.d\fR;
implemented in \fIsrc/kernel/d/core/syscalls/posix.d\fR.
.SH CAVEAT
This kernel emulates a SUBSET of the Linux ABI.  Behaviour that stock Linux
guarantees is not guaranteed here unless the DESCRIPTION says so.  Notably,
AF_UNIX reads return EAGAIN on an empty socket rather than blocking, and
absolute opens are resolved against the calling task's namespace.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR anonymos-syscalls (7)
